data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 10, the Cosmos DB provider allowed synchronous LINQ by opting into sync-over-async (e.g., `CosmosOptionsExtension` with `AllowSynchronousIO`). **In .NET 11, that opt-in is removed entirely.** All synchronous query and save operations on the Cosmos provider now throw `InvalidOperationException` at runtime.

**Every method in your repository breaks:**

| Method | Throws because |
|---|---|
| `ToList()` | Sync query execution removed |
| `First(...)` | Sync query execution removed |
| `Count()` | Sync query execution removed |
| `SaveChanges()` | Sync save removed |

## The Fix: Go Fully Async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key steps:**
1. Remove any `AllowSynchronousIO = true` configuration — it's no longer recognized.
2. Convert all repository methods to `async Task<T>` / `async Task`.
3. Propagate `async/await` up through callers (controllers, services, etc.).
4. Use the `Async` LINQ variants (`ToListAsync`, `FirstAsync`, `CountAsync`, etc.) from `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore`.

The Cosmos SDK has always been async-only under the hood — sync-over-async was a compatibility shim that risked deadlocks. .NET 11 removes the shim entirely.
